  "details": "EDIT: The below behavior is explained by IK Execution Order completely overriding the way the IK solvers execute. This can be worked around by disabling your avatar's execution order and enabling your own (on a separate object), or by *only* defining the VR IK component in the execution order. Final IK has undocumented behavior where other IK solvers will implicitly solve after anything defined in execution order.\n\nThe current open beta seems to have fixed the issue where additional IK solvers would make your footsteps act strangely.\n\nHowever, I can now no longer turn off my IK solvers (such as extra FABRIK components) when using IK Execution Order. Even if I disable the FABRIK component or disable the target object, the solver remains on.\n\nIf I move the FABRIK script to another disabled object, the FABRIK solver still remains on. If I *also* move the IK Execution Order script to this new object, the FABRIK becomes toggle-able, but also makes my avatar tap their feet very rapidly (like the old behavior).",
